==============================================================================
PART 1.  T7 -- No Frobenius-stable / multiplicatively-invariant weak keys
         (exhaustive verification for the small primes, proof for all m prime)
==============================================================================
  Frobenius-map self-test (v -> v^2 == GF2k.mul(v,v)) for m=5,7,11 : PASS
  m=5 (prime): enumerated 372 subspaces of dim 1..4 ; Frobenius-stable ones: 2 [1, 4]
  m=7 (prime): enumerated 29210 subspaces of dim 1..6 ; Frobenius-stable ones: 6 [1, 3, 3, 4, 4, 6]
  Exact structure (normal basis theorem): GF(2^m) is a CYCLIC F2[t]-module
  under t = Frobenius, isomorphic to F2[t]/(t^m-1).  Hence the Frobenius-stable
  F2-subspaces are exactly the ideals, i.e. the divisors of t^m-1 over GF(2),
  and the possible dimensions are the DEGREES of those divisors:
      { deg(g) : g | t^m-1 } = { sum over e|m of k_e * ord_e(2) }.
  (m=5 above: ord_5(2)=4, divisors of t^5-1=(t-1)*Phi_5 have degrees {0,1,5}
   -- but dim 1 is <spanned by 1> and dim 4 is the TRACE-ZERO hyperplane; both
   are Frobenius stable, so the naive 'no stable subspace' claim is FALSE.)

  VERIFICATION of the divisor characterisation at small m (exhaustive):
     m= 5 : observed stable dims [1, 4]   predicted [1, 4]   MATCH=True
     m= 7 : observed stable dims [1, 3, 4, 6]   predicted [1, 3, 4, 6]   MATCH=True

  THE REAL PARAMETERS (all m prime):
  instance         m   d ord_m(2)     Frobenius-stable dims        d-dim stable F exists?
  ROLLO-I-128     67   8 66           [0, 1, 66, 67]               False
  ROLLO-I-192     79   8 39           [0, 1, 39, 40, 78, 79]       False
  ROLLO-I-256     97   9 48           [0, 1, 48, 49, 96, 97]       False

  T7 (multiplicative invariance -- the version that IS true):
  Stab_{K*}(F) = {c in K* : cF subseteq F}.  If c in Stab and c not in F2 then
  F is closed under F2[c] = K (m prime), so F in {0,K}.  Hence for every F with
  1 <= dim F < m :  Stab_{K*}(F) = {1}.
     m=5 : over ALL 372 subspaces F (1<=dim<m), #F with Stab_{K*}(F) != {1} : 0
     m=7 : over ALL 29210 subspaces F (1<=dim<m), #F with Stab_{K*}(F) != {1} : 0

