==============================================================================
PART 4.  Exact weak-key fractions (Gaussian binomials, exact big integers)
==============================================================================
  For a fixed known D-dim window W the covered class is
     W_D(W) = { F in Gr_d(K) : exists gamma in K*,  F subseteq gamma*W }.
  Scale invariance (T3) means ONE window covers all 2^m-1 scalings at once.

  instance         m   d     D | log2 |Gr_d(K)| log2 |W_D(W)|  log2 frac 
  ROLLO-I-128     67   8     8 |         473.79          67.00     -406.8
  ROLLO-I-192     79   8     8 |         569.79          79.00     -490.8
  ROLLO-I-256     97   9     9 |         793.79          97.00     -696.8

  Upper bound for D > d (each gamma contributes [D choose d]_2 subspaces):
     D= 8 : log2 |W_D| <=    67.00   log2 fraction <=   -406.79   (window matrix 59x8)
     D= 9 : log2 |W_D| <=    76.00   log2 fraction <=   -397.79   (window matrix 58x9)
     D=10 : log2 |W_D| <=    84.41   log2 fraction <=   -389.38   (window matrix 57x10)
     D=13 : log2 |W_D| <=   108.74   log2 fraction <=   -365.05   (window matrix 54x13)
     D=16 : log2 |W_D| <=   132.78   log2 fraction <=   -341.01   (window matrix 51x16)
     D=33 : log2 |W_D| <=   268.79   log2 fraction <=   -205.00   (window matrix 34x33)

==============================================================================
PART 5.  T6 -- Window Covering Bound (why this is inherently a WEAK-KEY attack)
==============================================================================
  Any family Fm of D-dim windows that contains, for EVERY F in Gr_d(K), at least
  one W with F subseteq W must have
        |Fm|  >=  [2^m-1 choose d]_2  /  [2^(m-d) choose D-d]_2 .
     ROLLO-I-128    D=9 : |Fm| >= 2^414.8  windows  (=> no sub-exponential full attack)
     ROLLO-I-192    D=9 : |Fm| >= 2^498.8  windows  (=> no sub-exponential full attack)
     ROLLO-I-256    D=10 : |Fm| >= 2^705.8  windows  (=> no sub-exponential full attack)

==============================================================================
PART 6.  T9 -- DFR structure: dim(EF) profile at the real parameters
==============================================================================
  ROLLO spec v2.0 Prop 2.4.3:  DFR ~ q^{-(d-1)(m-r'-r)} + q^{-(n-r'+1)},  r'=dim EF.
  Both exponents are INCREASING in r', so the DFR is MAXIMISED at the generic
  r' = r*d.  Low-dimension F*E intersections therefore make decryption MORE
  reliable, not less -- the opposite of a DFR-amplification weakness.

  instance         m   n   r    d | term1     term2     DFR(spec) log2 Pr[r'<rd]
  ROLLO-I-128     67  83   7    8 | 2^-28     2^-28     2^-28     2^-11      
  ROLLO-I-192     79  97   8    8 | 2^-49     2^-34     2^-34     2^-15      
  ROLLO-I-256     97 113   9    9 | 2^-56     2^-33     2^-33     2^-16      

  (Predicted log2 Pr[dim<EF> < r*d] = -(m - r*d); verified by simulation below.)
  SIMULATION ROLLO-I-128: 5/4000 random (F,E) pairs have dim<EF> < r*d = 56
      predicted 0.0005 = 2^-11 ;   observed rate 0.00125      [8.0s]

